@nordic-piks, it looks like GCC optimized out `if { memcpy() }` branch and only `print_u32()` are left at  `write_u64()`.
My first quick fix was wrapping this function into '-O0' like this:
```
#pragma GCC push_options
#pragma GCC optimize("O0")
static inline void write_u64( ... ) {
...
}
#pragma GCC pop_options
```
